#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Introduction {#1-introduction}"
msgstr "1. Pengenalan {#1-introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a real time evolution technique, Trotterization consists in the successive application of a quantum gate or gates, chosen to approximate the time evolution of a system for a time slice. Following from the Schrödinger equation, the time evolution of a system initially in the state $\\vert\\psi(0)\\rangle$ takes the form:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai teknik evolusi masa nyata, Trotterisasi terdiri daripada penggunaan berturutan satu atau lebih gate kuantum yang dipilih untuk menghampiri evolusi masa sistem bagi satu hirisan masa. Berdasarkan persamaan Schrödinger, evolusi masa sistem yang bermula dalam keadaan $\\vert\\psi(0)\\rangle$ mengambil bentuk:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle = e^{-i H t} \\vert \\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle = e^{-i H t} \\vert \\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $H$ is the time-independent Hamiltonian governing the system. We consider a Hamiltonian that can be written as a weighted sum of Pauli terms $H=\\sum_j a_j P_j$, with $P_j$ representing a tensor product of Pauli terms acting on $n$ qubits. In particular, these Pauli terms might commute with one another, or they might not. Given a state at time $t=0$, how do we obtain the system's state at a later time $|\\psi(t)\\rangle$ using a quantum computer? The exponential of an operator can be most easily understood through its Taylor series:\n"
msgstr "di mana $H$ ialah Hamiltonian tak bersandar masa yang mengawal sistem. Kita mempertimbangkan Hamiltonian yang boleh ditulis sebagai jumlah berwajaran bagi sebutan Pauli $H=\\sum_j a_j P_j$, dengan $P_j$ mewakili hasil darab tensor sebutan Pauli yang bertindak ke atas $n$ qubit. Khususnya, sebutan-sebutan Pauli ini mungkin bertukar ganti antara satu sama lain, atau mungkin tidak. Diberi keadaan pada masa $t=0$, bagaimana kita mendapatkan keadaan sistem pada masa kemudian $|\\psi(t)\\rangle$ menggunakan komputer kuantum? Eksponen bagi satu operator paling mudah difahami melalui siri Taylornya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-iHt-\\frac{1}{2}H^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-iHt-\\frac{1}{2}H^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Some very basic exponentials, like $e^{iZ}$ can be implemented easily on quantum computers using a compact set of quantum gates. Most Hamiltonians of interest will not have just a single term, but will instead have many terms. Note what happens if $H = H_1+H_2$:\n"
msgstr "Sesetengah eksponen yang sangat asas, seperti $e^{iZ}$ boleh dilaksanakan dengan mudah pada komputer kuantum menggunakan set gate kuantum yang ringkas. Kebanyakan Hamiltonian yang menarik tidak akan mempunyai hanya satu sebutan, tetapi akan mempunyai banyak sebutan. Perhatikan apa yang berlaku jika $H = H_1+H_2$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-i(H_1+H_2)t-\\frac{1}{2}(H_1+H_2)^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i H t} = 1-i(H_1+H_2)t-\\frac{1}{2}(H_1+H_2)^2t^2+...\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When $H_1$ and $H_2$ commute, we have the familiar case (which is also true for numbers, and variables $a$ and $b$ below):\n"
msgstr "Apabila $H_1$ dan $H_2$ bertukar ganti, kita mempunyai kes biasa (yang juga benar untuk nombor, dan pemboleh ubah $a$ dan $b$ di bawah):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (a+b) t} = e^{-i a t}e^{-i b t}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (a+b) t} = e^{-i a t}e^{-i b t}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But when operators do not commute, terms cannot be rearranged in the Taylor series to simplify in this way. Thus, expressing complicated Hamiltonians in quantum gates is a challenge.\n"
msgstr "Tetapi apabila pengendali tidak bertukar ganti, sebutan-sebutan tidak boleh disusun semula dalam siri Taylor untuk disederhanakan dengan cara ini. Oleh itu, menyatakan Hamiltonian yang rumit dalam gate kuantum merupakan satu cabaran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One solution is to consider very small time $t$, such that the first-order term in the Taylor expansion dominates. Under that assumption:\n"
msgstr "Satu penyelesaian ialah mempertimbangkan masa $t$ yang sangat kecil, supaya sebutan peringkat pertama dalam pengembangan Taylor mendominasi. Di bawah andaian itu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (H_1+H_2) t} \\approx 1-i(H_1+H_2)t \\approx (1-i H_1 t)(1-i H_2 t) \\approx e^{-i H_1 t}e^{-i H_2 t}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-i (H_1+H_2) t} \\approx 1-i(H_1+H_2)t \\approx (1-i H_1 t)(1-i H_2 t) \\approx e^{-i H_1 t}e^{-i H_2 t}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, we might need to evolve our state for a longer time. That is accomplished by using many such small steps in time. This process is called Trotterization:\n"
msgstr "Tentu saja, kita mungkin perlu mengembangkan keadaan kita untuk masa yang lebih lama. Ini dicapai dengan menggunakan banyak langkah kecil dalam masa. Proses ini dipanggil Trotterisasi:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle \\approx \\left(\\prod_j e^{-i a_j P_j t/r} \\right)^r \\vert\\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi(t) \\rangle \\approx \\left(\\prod_j e^{-i a_j P_j t/r} \\right)^r \\vert\\psi(0) \\rangle \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here $t/r$ is the time slice (evolution step) that we are choosing. As a result, a gate to be applied $r$ times is created. A smaller timestep leads to a more accurate approximation. However, this also leads to deeper circuits which, in practice, leads to more error accumulation (a non-negligible concern on near-term quantum devices).\n"
msgstr "Di sini $t/r$ ialah hirisan masa (langkah evolusi) yang kita pilih. Hasilnya, satu gate dicipta untuk digunakan sebanyak $r$ kali. Langkah masa yang lebih kecil menghasilkan penghampiran yang lebih tepat. Walau bagaimanapun, ini juga menghasilkan litar yang lebih dalam yang, dalam amalan, membawa kepada pengumpulan ralat yang lebih banyak (satu kebimbangan yang tidak boleh diabaikan pada peranti kuantum jangka hampir).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Today, we will study the time evolution of the [Ising model](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ising_model) on linear lattices of $N=2$ and $N=6$ sites. These lattices consist of an array of spins $\\sigma_i$ that interact only with their nearest neighbors. These spins can have two orientations: $\\uparrow$ and $\\downarrow$, which correspond to a magnetization of $+1$ and $-1$ respectively.\n"
msgstr "Hari ini, kita akan mengkaji evolusi masa [model Ising](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ising_model) pada kekisi linear bersaiz $N=2$ dan $N=6$. Kekisi ini terdiri daripada susunan spin $\\sigma_i$ yang hanya berinteraksi dengan jiran terdekat mereka. Spin-spin ini boleh mempunyai dua orientasi: $\\uparrow$ dan $\\downarrow$, yang masing-masing sepadan dengan magnetisasi $+1$ dan $-1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = - J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} - h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} X_i  \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = - J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} - h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} X_i  \\text{,}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $J$ describes the interaction energy, and $h$ the magnitude of an external field (in the x-direction above, but we will modify this). Let us write this expression using Pauli matrices, and considering that the external field has an angle $\\alpha$ with respect to the transversal direction,\n"
msgstr "di mana $J$ menggambarkan tenaga interaksi, dan $h$ magnitud medan luar (dalam arah x di atas, tetapi kita akan mengubah ini). Mari kita tulis ungkapan ini menggunakan matriks Pauli, dan mempertimbangkan bahawa medan luar membuat sudut $\\alpha$ terhadap arah melintang,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} -h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} (\\sin\\alpha Z_i + \\cos\\alpha X_i) \\text{.}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -J \\sum_{i=0}^{N-2} Z_i Z_{i+1} -h \\sum_{i=0}^{N-1} (\\sin\\alpha Z_i + \\cos\\alpha X_i) \\text{.}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This Hamiltonian is useful in that it allows us to easily study the effects of an external field. In the computational basis, the system will be encoded as follows:\n"
msgstr "Hamiltonian ini berguna kerana ia membolehkan kita mengkaji dengan mudah kesan medan luar. Dalam asas pengiraan, sistem akan dikodkan seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Quantum state            | Spin representation                        |\n"
"|:------------------------:|:------------------------------------------:|\n"
"| $\\lvert 0 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$         |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$       |\n"
"| $\\ldots$                 | $\\ldots$                                   |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 1 1 1 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Keadaan kuantum          | Perwakilan spin                            |\n"
"|:------------------------:|:------------------------------------------:|\n"
"| $\\lvert 0 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$         |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 0 0 0 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$       |\n"
"| $\\ldots$                 | $\\ldots$                                   |\n"
"| $\\lvert 1 1 1 1 \\rangle$ | $\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\downarrow$ |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will start investigating the time evolution of such a quantum system. More specifically, we will visualize the time-evolution of certain properties of the system like magnetization.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mula mengkaji evolusi masa sistem kuantum sedemikian. Lebih khusus lagi, kita akan memvisualisasikan evolusi masa sifat-sifat tertentu sistem seperti magnetisasi.\n"

