#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Mapping your problem {#2-mapping-your-problem}"
msgstr "2. Pemetaan masalah anda {#2-mapping-your-problem}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.1 Defining the transverse-field Ising Hamiltonian {#21-defining-the-transverse-field-ising-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "2.1 Mendefinisikan Hamiltonian Ising medan transversal {#21-defining-the-transverse-field-ising-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We here consider the 1-D transverse-field Ising model.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita mempertimbangkan model Ising medan transversal 1-D.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we will create a function that takes in the system parameters $N$, $J$, $h$ and $\\alpha$, and returns our Hamiltonian as a `SparsePauliOp`. A [SparsePauliOp](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp) is a sparse representation of an operator in terms of weighted [Pauli](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Pauli) terms.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, kita akan membuat fungsi yang menerima parameter sistem $N$, $J$, $h$ dan $\\alpha$, dan mengembalikan Hamiltonian kita sebagai `SparsePauliOp`. Sebuah [SparsePauliOp](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp) ialah perwakilan jarang bagi pengendali dalam sebutan [Pauli](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Pauli) berwajaran.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Definisikan Hamiltonian {#define-the-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The system that we now consider has a size of $N=6$, $J=0.2$, $h=1.2$ and $\\alpha=\\frac{\\pi}{8.0}$ as an example.\n"
msgstr "Sistem yang kita pertimbangkan sekarang mempunyai saiz $N=6$, $J=0.2$, $h=1.2$ dan $\\alpha=\\frac{\\pi}{8.0}$ sebagai contoh.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.2 Set the parameters of the time-evolution simulation {#22-set-the-parameters-of-the-time-evolution-simulation}"
msgstr "2.2 Tetapkan parameter simulasi evolusi masa {#22-set-the-parameters-of-the-time-evolution-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we will consider three different Trotterization techniques:\n"
"* Lie–Trotter (first order)\n"
"* second-order Suzuki–Trotter\n"
"* fourth-order Suzuki–Trotter\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita akan mempertimbangkan tiga teknik Trotterisasi yang berbeza:\n"
"* Lie–Trotter (peringkat pertama)\n"
"* Suzuki–Trotter peringkat kedua\n"
"* Suzuki–Trotter peringkat keempat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The latter two will be used in the exercise, and in the appendix.\n"
msgstr "Dua yang terakhir akan digunakan dalam latihan, dan dalam lampiran.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.3 Prepare the quantum circuit 1 (Initial state) {#23-prepare-the-quantum-circuit-1-initial-state}"
msgstr "2.3 Sediakan litar kuantum 1 (Keadaan awal) {#23-prepare-the-quantum-circuit-1-initial-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Create an initial state. Here we will start with a spin configuration of $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$\n"
".\n"
msgstr "Cipta keadaan awal. Di sini kita akan bermula dengan konfigurasi spin $\\uparrow\\uparrow\\downarrow\\downarrow\\uparrow\\uparrow$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/quantum-simulation/extracted-outputs/b338806d-67bf-47ae-9d03-944bde3e2c99-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/quantum-simulation/extracted-outputs/b338806d-67bf-47ae-9d03-944bde3e2c99-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.4 Prepare the quantum circuit 2 (Single circuit for time evolution) {#24-prepare-the-quantum-circuit-2-single-circuit-for-time-evolution}"
msgstr "2.4 Sediakan litar kuantum 2 (litar tunggal untuk evolusi masa) {#24-prepare-the-quantum-circuit-2-single-circuit-for-time-evolution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We here construct a circuit for a single time step using Lie–Trotter.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita membina satu litar untuk satu langkah masa menggunakan Lie–Trotter.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Lie product formula (first-order) is implemented in the [LieTrotter](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) class. A first-order formula consists of the approximation stated in the introduction, where the matrix exponential of a sum is approximated by a product of matrix exponentials:\n"
msgstr "Formula hasil Lie (peringkat pertama) dilaksanakan dalam kelas [LieTrotter](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter). Formula peringkat pertama terdiri daripada penghampiran yang dinyatakan dalam pengenalan, di mana eksponen matriks bagi satu jumlah dihampiri dengan hasil darab eksponen matriks:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{H_1+H_2} \\approx e^{H_1} e^{H_2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{H_1+H_2} \\approx e^{H_1} e^{H_2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As previously mentioned, very deep circuits lead to the accumulation of errors, and cause problems for modern quantum computers. Because two-qubit gates have higher error rates than single-qubit gates, a quantity of particular interest is the two-qubit circuit depth. What really matters is the two-qubit circuit depth after transpilation (since that is the circuit the quantum computer actually executes). But let us get in the habit of counting the operations for this circuit, even now using the simulator.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang disebutkan sebelumnya, litar yang sangat dalam membawa kepada pengumpulan ralat, dan menyebabkan masalah bagi komputer kuantum moden. Kerana gate dua-qubit mempunyai kadar ralat yang lebih tinggi daripada gate satu-qubit, satu kuantiti yang amat menarik ialah kedalaman litar dua-qubit. Apa yang benar-benar penting ialah kedalaman litar dua-qubit selepas transpilasi (kerana itulah litar yang sebenarnya dilaksanakan oleh komputer kuantum). Tetapi mari kita biasakan diri mengira operasi untuk litar ini, walaupun sekarang menggunakan simulator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/quantum-simulation/extracted-outputs/252c2734-653d-4c8e-af6b-d3173845de88-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/quantum-simulation/extracted-outputs/252c2734-653d-4c8e-af6b-d3173845de88-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.5 Set the operators to measure {#25-set-the-operators-to-measure}"
msgstr "2.5 Tetapkan pengendali untuk diukur {#25-set-the-operators-to-measure}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us define a *magnetization operator* $\\sum_i \\langle Z_i \\rangle / N$, and a *mean spin correlation operator* $\\sum_i \\langle Z_i Z_{i+1} \\rangle/ (N - 1)$.\n"
msgstr "Mari kita definisikan *pengendali magnetisasi* $\\sum_i \\langle Z_i \\rangle / N$, dan *pengendali korelasi spin purata* $\\sum_i \\langle Z_i Z_{i+1} \\rangle/ (N - 1)$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.6 Perform time-evolution simulation {#26-perform-time-evolution-simulation}"
msgstr "2.6 Jalankan simulasi evolusi masa {#26-perform-time-evolution-simulation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will monitor the energy (expectation value of the Hamiltonian), magnetization (expectation value of the magnetization operator), and mean spin correlation (expectation value of the mean spin correlation operator). Qiskit's `StatevectorEstimator` (EstimatorV2) primitive estimates expectation values of observables, $\\langle\\psi\\vert\\hat{O}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan memantau tenaga (nilai jangkaan Hamiltonian), magnetisasi (nilai jangkaan pengendali magnetisasi), dan korelasi spin purata (nilai jangkaan pengendali korelasi spin purata). `StatevectorEstimator` (EstimatorV2) Qiskit menganggar nilai jangkaan bagi kuantiti boleh cerap (observable), $\\langle\\psi\\vert\\hat{O}\\vert\\psi\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "2.7 Plot the time evolution of the observables {#27-plot-the-time-evolution-of-the-observables}"
